# Review screenshots. Evidence for one visual review, not repository content:
# they go stale the moment the interface changes, and a binary that nobody
# diffs does not belong in git history.
# Excluded as `artifacts/*` rather than `artifacts/`: a trailing slash makes git
# skip the directory outright, and a negation cannot re-include anything inside
# a directory git never descended into.
artifacts/*
# ...except the two review deliverables, which are the evidence that the
# interface was checked in a real browser rather than reasoned about. The
# contact sheet is ~540KB and the audit is text; the 27 full-page screenshots
# behind them are ~4MB and are regenerated by `scripts/capture-ui-screenshots.mjs`,
# so they stay out.
!artifacts/ui-review/
artifacts/ui-review/*
!artifacts/ui-review/00-contact-sheet.png
!artifacts/ui-review/INTERACTION_AUDIT.md
# ...and the load measurement, for the same reason: it is the evidence, and it
# is text. The raw Playwright traces and screenshots stay out.
!artifacts/load/
artifacts/load/*
!artifacts/load/HTTP_LOAD.md

# Review-server secrets, generated locally by scripts/review-server.mjs.
.env.review.local
